---
import CaseSection
  from "../components/case-study/CaseSection.astro";

import CaseMedia
  from "../components/case-study/CaseMedia.astro";
---

<CaseSection
  number="01"
  label="Problem"
  title="Helping academic staff identify students who may require attention."
>
  <p>
    This case study will eventually focus more heavily
    on system logic, user roles, data, and development
    than visual exploration.
  </p>
</CaseSection>


<section class="site-container">
  <CaseMedia
    label="System overview"
    caption="Placeholder for a high-level system or user-flow diagram."
    tone="dark"
  />
</section>


<CaseSection
  number="02"
  label="System Design"
  title="Different responsibilities required different views of the same academic data."
>
  <p>
    The final content can explain the relationship
    between user roles, student information, academic
    warning conditions, and notification workflows.
  </p>
</CaseSection>


<section
  class="site-container grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-12"
>
  <div class="md:col-span-7">
    <CaseMedia
      label="Dashboard"
      caption="Placeholder for the main monitoring interface."
      ratio="landscape"
      tone="panel"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="md:col-span-5">
    <CaseMedia
      label="Notification"
      caption="Placeholder for email-warning workflow or interface."
      ratio="portrait"
      tone="light"
    />
  </div>
</section>


<CaseSection
  number="03"
  label="Technical Layer"
  title="Designing the interface while also building the underlying feature."
>
  <p>
    This is where the final case study can explain
    relevant implementation decisions, data handling,
    database relationships, and technical constraints
    without turning the portfolio into code
    documentation.
  </p>
</CaseSection>


<section class="site-container">
  <CaseMedia
    label="Architecture / Data"
    caption="Placeholder for simplified technical architecture."
    tone="dark"
  />
</section>